// Title: Suspicious Keyboard Layout Load
// Sigma ID: 34aa0252-6039-40ff-951f-939fd6ce47d8
// Status: test | Level: medium
// Author: Florian Roth (Nextron Systems)
// Date: 2019-10-12 | Modified: 2023-08-17
// ATT&CK: resource-development, T1588.002
// Description: Detects the keyboard preload installation with a suspicious keyboard layout, e.g. Chinese,
//   Iranian or Vietnamese layout load in user session on systems maintained by US staff only
// False positives:
//   - Administrators or users that actually use the selected keyboard layouts (heavily depends on the organisation's user base)
// References:
//   - https://renenyffenegger.ch/notes/Windows/registry/tree/HKEY_CURRENT_USER/Keyboard-Layout/Preload/index
//   - https://github.com/SwiftOnSecurity/sysmon-config/pull/92/files
// Sigma rule: https://github.com/SigmaHQ/sigma/blob/ccbb0369507f796db0b0ae6854c8a2be471b9d84/rules/windows/registry/registry_set/registry_set_susp_keyboard_layout_load.yml
// License: Detection Rule License (DRL) 1.1 - https://github.com/SigmaHQ/Detection-Rule-License
// Converted by sigma2kql (target: microsoft_xdr, pySigma 1.5.1, pySigma-backend-kusto 1.0.1)
// Validation: passed (Kusto.Language 12.4.1, live Defender schema)
// Machine-generated and not tested against real telemetry. Verify before use as a detection.
// Note: 2 wildcard comparison(s) rewritten to 'matches regex' (KQL treats * in contains/endswith/== as a literal character)

DeviceRegistryEvents
| where (RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Keyboard Layout\\Preload.*$" or RegistryKey matches regex @"(?i)\\Keyboard Layout\\Substitutes.*$") and (RegistryValueData contains "00000429" or RegistryValueData contains "00050429" or RegistryValueData contains "0000042a")
